Slackware Post-Install Scripts (PIS)

'Let the Slackers be a little bit lazy. ;)'

PIS is a dialog-based assistant for selected Slackware 15.0
post-installation tasks on x86 and x86_64. It configures locale,
keyboards, date/time, optional NTP synchronization, login mode,
users, wheel administration, X sessions, ELILO/LILO/GRUB kernels,
slackpkg mirrors and selected package-management tools.

Version 0.5.0 validates changes, displays the current configuration,
creates automatic backups and supports restoration. Its portable
profiles store mirror URLs and never contain passwords.

PIS changes standard Slackware configuration files. Backups are stored
under /var/log/PIS/backups and can be restored from the PIS menu or with
"pis --restore". Kernel configuration is offered when ELILO, LILO or
GRUB is detected. Repository choices follow the detected Slackware
branch and architecture. Prebuilt slapt tools are limited to 15.0.

For GRUB, PIS creates explicit top-level entries for the selected
kernels and asks which one should be the default. Automatically
detected GRUB entries are kept as fallback choices.

PIS does not replace Slackware's native network and service tools.

This SlackBuild targets a full, patched Slackware 15.0 installation.
Upstream PIS also detects Slackware-current, but current is outside the
support scope of SlackBuilds.org.

No additional build dependencies are required on a full Slackware 15.0
installation. Some optional package-manager actions need Internet access
and can download third-party tools only after explicit confirmation.

After installing the package, run "pis" as root. Review the displayed
changes before confirming them. PIS stores restorable backups under
/var/log/PIS/backups.
